# Line endings in this directory are not a matter of taste.
#
# RMAC silently skips a source block whose lines end in LF alone.  It
# reports no error: the module assembles to a plausible size with lines
# missing, and the fault shows up only on hardware.  Everything here that
# is assembled with RMAC must therefore reach the working tree as CRLF.
#
# cpm3.asm is the exception.  It is assembled with ez80asm, which expects
# LF, so it is listed again below to override the *.asm rule above it.

*               text=auto

# RMAC and DRLINK sources -- MUST be CRLF
*.asm           text eol=crlf
*.lib           text eol=crlf

# ez80asm source and host tools -- LF
cpm3.asm        text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

# Binaries.  gencpm.dat is listed because it contains no NUL and no byte
# above 126, so git would otherwise treat it as text and rewrite the CRLF
# pairs inside it, corrupting GENCPM's saved answers.
*.com           binary
*.spr           binary
*.dat           binary
